VERDESK - END USER LICENSE AGREEMENT

Version 1.4 - Effective from Verdesk 2.62.0

This is not a contract full of fine print: it is written to be understood. If
you install or use Verdesk, you accept this agreement. If you do not agree, do
not install or use it.

This agreement is between you and Camilo Brossard, who develops and sells
Verdesk ("Verdesk", "we", "us").


1. WHAT VERDESK IS AND WHAT YOU ARE BUYING

Verdesk is a Windows program that lets an AI, or another program, see and
operate your computer: it looks at the screen, reads text, clicks, types, drives
a web browser and runs commands.

   - Free. No charge, for personal use, study and any other use that is not
     commercial.
   - Pro. A monthly subscription of USD 2.90. It is paid with PayPal at
     pay.verdesk.app and renews by itself every month until you cancel it. It
     adds the Pro features (macros, saved buttons and objects, drafts and access
     from other computers: Local (LAN) and Remote (WAN)) and the right to
     commercial use.
   - Up to 2 of your own computers per license. If you change computers, you can
     release your computers once every 30 days.
   - Trial. For the first 60 days you get full Pro, with no card and without
     asking for it. When it ends, Verdesk keeps working as Free.
   - If you cancel or a payment fails, your license stays Pro until the end of
     the period you already paid for, plus 7 days of margin. After that Verdesk
     goes back to Free. Nothing of yours is deleted.
   - You are buying the right to use Verdesk, not the program itself: the
     program remains ours.

2. VERDESK IS UNDER DEVELOPMENT

It will have bugs and some things will change. We publish fixes often, and
Verdesk tells you when a new version is available. If something breaks, write to
us.


3. WHAT VERDESK SEES STAYS ON YOUR COMPUTER

What Verdesk sees and does (screenshots, text it reads, windows, clipboard,
activity history, macros, objects and remembered passwords) is stored on your
computer, and Verdesk does not send it anywhere. There is no telemetry, no
analytics, no account and no sign-in.

The only things that leave your computer are these:

   1. The first-run sign-up. When you finish the welcome screens, your email,
      the version, the license type and a random identifier of this computer go
      to pay.verdesk.app, which forwards them to us by email, to the Verdesk
      mailbox and to its owner's mailbox. It happens once, and the email is
      required to finish the welcome screens.
   2. Reports. Only when you, or the AI you connected, send a report: the report
      text, its type, the version and the computer name. The connected AI can
      send a report on its own; it writes the text.
   3. A paid license. When you activate it, and afterwards only when needed
      (more than 7 days without checking, close to expiry, or after a notice
      from the server), Verdesk sends pay.verdesk.app your license, which
      carries your purchase email, the plan and the expiry date, and a computer
      identifier calculated with a hash, never the Windows one. The trial and
      Free never contact the license server. Without a connection, Verdesk keeps
      working.
   4. Updates. When it starts and every 24 hours, Verdesk asks GitHub which
      version is the latest; GitHub sees your IP address and your version. This
      check cannot be turned off: it is how fixes reach you in time. If you
      choose to install, Verdesk downloads the installer from GitHub and checks
      its fingerprint before opening it.
   5. Only if you turn on Local (LAN) or Remote (WAN). If OpenSSH is missing,
      Verdesk downloads it from GitHub (Microsoft's build) or installs it
      through Windows Update. In Remote, if you choose to install Tailscale, it
      downloads it from Tailscale. In both cases it checks the installer's
      signature before using it. In Remote, Verdesk also asks api.ipify.org for
      your public IP and asks your router (via UPnP) to open port 22 to this
      computer; while Remote stays on it checks every 30 minutes that the port
      is still open, and it closes it when you leave Remote, when you close it
      from Connection and when you uninstall.

Whatever the browser driven by Verdesk loads is what you or the AI ask it to
load: it is your browsing, not something Verdesk sends. Verdesk does not read
the cookies or the history of your browsers.


4. THE AI YOU CONNECT BELONGS TO SOMEONE ELSE

The AI you connect (Claude, ChatGPT, a model on your own computer or any other)
receives what Verdesk shows it: screenshots, text and pages. If that AI runs in
the cloud, that content leaves through its own program, under its own rules and
prices. We do not control what it does with it and we are not responsible for
its answers.

You choose which AI to connect, and you are responsible for what it does with
your computer through Verdesk. Review what it does, especially before anything
that cannot be undone.

In Local (LAN) and Remote (WAN), other computers can connect to this one. The
first connection from each computer asks for your approval, and Remote only lets
in a computer with a key. The connection text you copy for your AI contains what
is needed to get in: share it only with your own AI.


5. WHAT STAYS ON YOUR COMPUTER WHEN YOU UNINSTALL

When you uninstall, Verdesk removes what it opened: the firewall rules, the
router port and remote access.

Your license and your settings are kept on purpose, so you do not lose them if
you reinstall, and so is the 60-day trial marker, stored in several places on
your computer so that the trial cannot be repeated by reinstalling.

Your macros and objects, in Documents\Verdesk, are kept unless you agree to
delete them when the uninstaller asks.


6. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   - Use Free for commercial work.
   - Resell, rent, lend or share your license or your key.
   - Bypass, disable or trick the license or trial check, or use the Pro
     features without a license.
   - Decompile or reverse engineer the program, except where the law allows you
     to.
   - Use Verdesk on computers or accounts you are not allowed to use, to access
     systems or data without authorization, or for anything illegal.

If any of this happens, the license is cancelled without a refund.


7. REFUNDS

You have 14 days from your first purchase to ask for your money back. Write to
support@verdesk.app from the email you bought with and we refund you through
PayPal; you do not need to explain anything. When we refund your first purchase
we also cancel your subscription, so you are not charged again. Renewals are not
refunded, except for a charge made by mistake (for example, a duplicate one or
one made after you cancelled), which is refunded in full.


8. HOW FAR OUR RESPONSIBILITY GOES

We build this with care, but Verdesk is provided as is, without warranties of
any kind: we cannot guarantee that it works without failures on every computer
or in every case.

If something goes wrong through our fault, our liability is limited to what you
paid (on Free, nothing). We are not liable for lost data or work, time or
profits that did not happen, or for anything done by an AI or a program
connected to Verdesk.

Back up your work. That holds for any tool, not only this one.


9. CHANGES TO THIS AGREEMENT

If we change something important, we publish the new version with its date and
say so in the release notes. If you do not agree, you can cancel your
subscription and stop using Verdesk.


10. GOVERNING LAW

This agreement is governed by the laws of Chile. If any part is not valid, the
rest remains valid. It is the entire agreement between you and Verdesk about the
program.


11. CONTACT

support@verdesk.app - https://verdesk.app

Write to us about anything: problems, licenses, or if you need to move your
license to another computer.


